<title>NORWAY: Orkla share up on Oslo Bourse.</title>
<headline>Orkla share up on Oslo Bourse.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norwegian food-based conglomerate Orkla ASA was traded higher on Oslo Bourse on Friday following the release of strong 1996 results.</p>
<p>Orkla's A class share was up 18.50 crowns, or 3.64 percent, at 527 crowns in healthy trade worth 55 million crowns at 1300gmt.</p>
<p>The Total all-share index was up 0.76 percent.</p>
<p>Orkla said pre-tax profits increased by 29 percent because of gains in branded goods and the investment portfolio.</p>
<p>--Rolf Soderlind, Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
